analyses.4:
All 18 trials scored 0 on dev and 0 on training success. Every change tried scored 0: init hygiene, normalisation, raw-obs skips, factorised logits, gather and window heads, soft-AND lattices, the learned DONE gate (bias -2 or 0), symlog inputs, and recipes from 64 to 512 envs, 1 to 3 epochs and gamma 0.9 to 0.995. So none of these tests showed any advantage, and we still cannot tell any idea apart. The agent never finishes an exact build, so optimisation and inductive bias remain the bottleneck. This is the final round, so I use breadth. Untested axes:
- much larger capacity (r of about 4.5);
- a U-Net with a global receptive field;
- a per-layer lattice that sees the layer below and the missing cells below, which are needed for landing and sealing, with ordered footprint gathering;
- learned per-layer 3x3 context;
- legality-mask planes combined with a gather head;
- a learnable logit temperature.
The last candidate stacks all of them.
